      "side": 1,
      "message": "Note a subtle behavioral difference between Zephyr and legacy EC here when `mode` is `FP_MODE_FINGER_UP` (without `FP_MODE_ANY_WAIT_IRQ`):\n\n1. In non-Zephyr builds (`#ifndef CONFIG_ZEPHYR`), `GPIO_FPS_INT` is only enabled for `FP_MODE_ANY_WAIT_IRQ`, so `FP_MODE_FINGER_UP` is purely timer-polled (`FINGER_POLLING_DELAY \u003d 100ms`) with interrupts disabled.\n2. In Zephyr builds, `fp_configure_detect()` sets `FINGERPRINT_SENSOR_MODE_DETECT`, which enables the sensor GPIO IRQ in all Zephyr drivers (`fpc1025`, `fpc1145`, `egis630`, `egis660`, `elan_series`, `ft98xx`). Previously, calling `fp_sensor_low_power()` right after `fp_configure_detect()` happened to disable that IRQ again (except on `fpc1145`). With this change, the IRQ stays enabled when entering `FP_MODE_FINGER_UP`. On sensors where detect mode asserts the IRQ immediately when a finger is present, this will trigger an immediate `TASK_EVENT_SENSOR_IRQ` while the finger is still down (after which the ISR disables the IRQ and subsequent checks fall back to the 100ms timer).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 375,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 388,
        "endChar": 9999
      },
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "5de8e300a0818ee3334963b62e0844e648f84d6a",
